  ! Pool-flavored single-row read

getByLeagueId :: Pool -> Text -> IO (Either DBError (Maybe LeagueConfigRow))
  ! Pool-flavored user-id read

getAll :: Pool -> IO (Either DBError [LeagueConfigRow])
  ! Pool-flavored full read

%decision ScoringAndLimitsAsJsonbColumns
  what:    scoring_config (JSONB), roster_limits (JSONB), and lineup_limits (JSONB) are columns whose rel8 type is the Pelotero.DB.JsonB wrapper (JsonbScoring / JsonbRosterLimits / JsonbLineupLimits); the public LeagueConfigRow still carries the unwrapped Domain types
  why:     JSONB lets us evolve the inner record shape without a schema migration on every existing row. Phase A.4 moved the Aeson instances off Domain onto the wrappers; this module wraps in insertLeagueConfigT / updateLeagueConfigT and unwraps in fromResult, keeping the public API in Domain types and Domain itself Aeson-free.
  affects: leagueConfigSchema, fromResult, insertLeagueConfigT, updateLeagueConfigT

%decision StatusAsTextNotEnum
  what:    _lcStatus is Column f Text, not the LeagueStatus domain sum
  why:     Same rationale as ProviderName for the fetch log: tolerate legacy or unrecognised values without crashing reads. The layered domain type LeagueStatus exists as the canonical render/parse pair; this column being Text is the persistence-layer trade-off.
  affects: leagueConfigSchema


